From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 13:05:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 55/56] DADAO: implement aggregate (struct)
 parameter/return-value ABI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

contracts/abi/spec.md §2.4 (wiki DADAO-21-ABI §聚合类型参数/§聚合类型返回值,
ML-031a):

- HPA (homogeneous pointer aggregate, <= 4 pointer leaves): Direct, coerced
  to [N x ptr] -- CC_DADAO's existing CCIfPtr rule places each flattened
  leaf in the RB bank for free.
- HFA (homogeneous float/double aggregate): detected via the same
  flatten() recursion but explicitly NOT implemented -- DADAO has no RF
  register class / floating-point CodeGen support at all. Reports a
  compiler warning and falls back unchanged to the pre-existing
  DefaultABIInfo indirect(byval) classification (docs/issues.yaml:
  dadao-hfa-argument-not-implemented).
- Otherwise, <= 32 bytes: Direct, coerced to [ceil(size/8) x i64] (1-4
  opaque 8-byte blocks in the RD bank).
- Otherwise (> 32 bytes): Indirect, ByVal=false -- caller allocates a
  temporary and passes its address as a plain RB-bank pointer.
- Aggregate return <= 64 bits: Direct i64 (RD31), unconditional on
  HFA/HPA shape per wiki. > 64 bits: Indirect (hidden sret, lands in RB16
  for free since CGCall.cpp always visits it first).
- EmitVAArg: IsIndirect now follows the real classification (was
  hardcoded false, silently wrong for the new >32B indirect case);
  ForceRightAdjust is now false for aggregates (natural/left-justified
  placement, matching this file's own coercion padding direction) and
  unchanged (true) for scalars.

Added clang/test/CodeGen/DADAO/aggregate-abi.c (directed IR-level check of
the coerced signatures); tests/lit/E2E/agg_args_named.test and
agg_vararg_multislot.test (runtime QEMU+gem5 coverage, in the DADAO-0628
superproject) cover the same ground end to end.

